# Class setup: 0 turns off Bonjour so "expo start --offline" works on a shared network.
# Read by the Expo CLI only, not by the app.
EXPO_UNSTABLE_BONJOUR=0

# Address of our Next.js API (mc2-api) on the laptop. The phone sends every customers request here.
# Read in src/data/customers.ts. Use the laptop's Wi-Fi address, not localhost.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.23:3000

# Address of the Supabase project. The phone uses it for sign up, sign in and sign out only.
# Read in src/lib/supabase.ts.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ntyilnpnkwcdxltteyzc.supabase.co

# The project's publishable key (sb_publishable_...). It tells Supabase which project the app belongs to.
# Public by design, so it is safe inside the app. Never put a secret key or the database password here.
# Read in src/lib/supabase.ts.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_KEY=sb_publishable_uxL-Wzsmpi9DCDUsdw9cSw_V1EZOREG

